     "<div><div aria-label=\"Message Body\" role=\"textbox\" aria-multiline=\"true\" style=\"direction:ltr;min-height:376px\" aria-controls=\":2hz\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Dear respected members of the INLA community,</span><br></span><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I have been trying to use the BAPC/INLA to project age standardized rates. Using the model example set by the BAPC package and another by (</span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://github.com/jianglindmw/age-period-cohort-analysis-Primary-liver-cancer-in-China\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jianglindmw/age-period-cohort-analysis-Primary-liver-cancer-in-China&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792435686873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0y6TG5_-Hlj8nLeeta6duu\">https://github.com/jianglindmw/age-period-cohort-analysis-Primary-liver-cancer-in-China</a>) [BAPC example shown below]. I get the error &quot;<b>reached numerical limit</b>&quot;. INLA reruns with improved values then crashes. The problem goes away when &quot;stdweights&quot; are removed.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\">## Not run: \r\nif(requireNamespace(&quot;INLA&quot;, quietly = TRUE)) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\">{\r\n   require(INLA) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"> data(FemLCSweden) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"> data(FemPYSweden) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"> data(whostandard) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"> lc_sweden &lt;- APCList(FemLCSweden, FemPYSweden, gf=5) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"> result &lt;- BAPC(lc_sweden, predict=list(npredict=10, retro=TRUE),\r\n      secondDiff=FALSE, stdweight=whostandard[6:17,2], verbose=FALSE)\r\n} </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"> ## End(Not run)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Is this an INLA error or an error in BAPC compatibility? All packages BAPC, INLA, and R program are updated as per March 2024. </span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Thank you for your help and assistance,</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,monospace;box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"box-sizing:inherit;overflow:auto;font-size:12.6px;padding-left:1em;padding-right:1em\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></span></span><